<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xi'an Incident</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xian">Xi'an</a> Incident was the detention of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a> in Xi'an in December 1936 by his own generals Zhang Xueliang and Yang Hucheng, who wanted him to stop fighting the Communists and resist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. After about two weeks of negotiations, in which the Communists took part, Chiang was released. The incident led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-united-front">Second United Front</a> of Nationalists and Communists against Japan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xian-incident.jpg" alt="Xi'an Incident" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zhang_Xueliang,_Yang_Hucheng_and_Chiang_Kai-shek.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
